//
// @SUBJECT: filtered-loops
// @CLAIM: `for x in xs if cond { … }` filters in the loop header, so the body sees only the elements that pass.
// @SEEN-FROM: 00-vs-rust.html#filtered-loops
// @SCRIPT — the page's block is a top-level window.

// --- as shown on 00-vs-rust.html#filtered-loops (a verbatim window: `rule_tags.py fences`) ---
items = [3, -1, 4];
total = 0;
for x in items if x > 0 {
    total += x;
}
assert(total == 7, "only the positive elements were summed");
